<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καίπερ</span></b> , in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> always with a word between (exc.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καί περ πολλὰ παθόντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.224
				</span></i>
			); but one word in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> and Prose, and usu. in Trag. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>even</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ αὐτοί περ πονεώμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.70
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>although, albeit</i>, usu. c. part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ αὐτῇ περ νοεούσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.577
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ ἀχνύμενός περ ἑταίρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.125
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ πρίν περ θυμῷ μεμαώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.135
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ κήδεά περ πεπαθυίῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.555
				</span></i>
			: so in later Poets, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀχνύμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					8(7).4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				6.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ θοῦρός περ ὤν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					199.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. αὐθάδη φρονῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					907
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. οὐ στέργων ὅμως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					712
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. οὐ δύσοργος ὤν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					377
				</span></i>
			: preceded by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμως</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				495d
			</span></i>: the part. must freq. be supplied, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ θεός περ</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1203
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γιγνώσκω σαφῶς, κ.
			σκοτεινὸς</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤν</span>], 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήν γε σὴν αὐδὴν ὅμως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1326
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ μέμονάς γε, καὶ ὀψέ
			περ</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρυόμενος</span>], . . 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.247
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμνησαίμεθα Χάρμης, καὶ πρὸς
				δαίμονά περ</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαχούμενοι</span>] <i><span class="en">
				17.104
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγεις ἀληθῆ, κ. ἐκ μακροῦ
				Χρόνου</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγων</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1141
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ἔστιν ὧν δεῖ, κ. οὐ
				πολλῶν ἄπο,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καίπερ οὐ πολλῶν
				ὄντων</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				647
			</span></i>: with finite Verbs only as dub. l., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ.
				ἔχει</span> (leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καἴπερ</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				4.36
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ</span>. (leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καίτοι</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἐκεῖνό γε ᾤμην τι εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					219c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
